@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
title SysML interaction INT-01 - grant, data fault and recovery
actor TrafficDataSource as Source
participant "sensor : VehicleDetection\nBLK-02" as Sensor
participant "analysis : DensityAnalysis\nBLK-03" as Analysis
participant "controller : TrafficController\nBLK-04" as Controller
participant "signals : SignalController\nBLK-05" as Signals
participant "lights : TrafficLights[4]\nBLK-06" as Lights
Source -> Sensor : CountsFrame (each 1 s)
Sensor -> Analysis : validated CountsFrame
Analysis -> Controller : DensityFrame
Sensor -> Controller : dataFault + recoveryStreak
Signals -> Controller : safeBoundary at tick (startup/clearance done)
Controller -> Controller : ACT-03 eligible + rank + deadlines
Controller -> Signals : PhaseCommand (approach, greenSeconds, mode)
Signals -> Signals : ACT-09 validate command and clearance
Signals -> Lights : LampVector: one green, others red
Signals -> Controller : grantAccepted(i)
Controller -> Controller : ACT-08 mark served; advance ring pointer
... granted 10/20/30 s in Normal ...
Source -> Sensor : invalid/stale data during green
Sensor -> Controller : latch dataFault
note over Controller,Signals
Current grant remains frozen.
No new green while grant/clearance is active.
end note
Signals -> Lights : active yellow, others red (3 s)
Signals -> Lights : all red (1 s)
Signals -> Controller : safeBoundary
Controller -> Signals : Fallback grant: next eligible in ring, 10 s
Signals -> Lights : one green, others red
loop three consecutive new valid frames on distinct ticks
 Source -> Sensor : CountsFrame with new observedAt
 Sensor -> Analysis : validated CountsFrame
 Analysis -> Controller : DensityFrame
 Sensor -> Controller : recoveryStreak; clear fault after third good frame
end
note over Controller
Sensor clears fault after 3 new good frames.
Controller returns Normal only at next round boundary.
No reset of round or wait timers on mode change.
end note
@enduml
